{"name":"Double Duty","hex":"#686858","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"double duty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The performance of two distinct roles simultaneously or the undertaking of work for two people.","A cryptic device or cluing error whereby a term forms part of both the definition and the wordplay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double_duty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Double Duty","blocks":[{"text":"Double Duty is an American auto racing term used to describe one of the most difficult feats in motorsport: in a single day, competing in both the Indianapolis 500 IndyCar Series race at Indianapolis Motor Speedway and the Coca-Cola 600 NASCAR Cup Series race at Charlotte Motor Speedway."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tony_stewart_%2851221641988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Tony_stewart_%2851221641988%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_Duty"},{"title":"Duty","blocks":[{"text":"A duty is a commitment or expectation to perform some action in general or if certain circumstances arise. A duty may arise from a system of ethics or morality, especially in an honor culture. Many duties are created by law, sometimes including a codified punishment or liability for non-performance. Performing one's duty may require some sacrifice of self-interest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Leighton-Duty-1883.jpg/330px-Leighton-Duty-1883.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duty"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Lowesmotorspeedway.jpg/500px-Lowesmotorspeedway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Lowesmotorspeedway.jpg/500px-Lowesmotorspe